<!-- HERO -->
<header class="post-hero">
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag tag-purple">Speculative Decoding</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Training Efficiency</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
    <span class="tag tag-amber">Systems</span>
  </div>
  <h1>SpecForge: Training Efficiency for Speculative Decoding Drafters</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Naive FSDP/ZeRO wraps a frozen trillion-parameter target model inside gradient-tracking machinery it will never use — inflating training time and killing MoE scalability. SpecForge decouples target inference (SGLang) from draft training (FSDP), adds FlexAttention for sparse tree attention, and contributes an in-place gradient kernel — delivering up to <strong>9.99× throughput on Qwen3-235B</strong>.
  </p>
  <div class="post-hero-meta">
