<p>
  The contrast is stark: on the left, the frozen target's parameters are either replicated across all eight GPUs (ZeRO-2) or constantly all-gathered before each inference step (ZeRO-3). Neither is the inference pattern that SGLang uses natively. On the right, the target model is handled entirely by SGLang — with its own tensor parallelism, FlashAttention-3 kernels, and CUDA Graphs — while the draft model gets a lean ZeRO Stage 2 that only shards optimizer states and gradients.
</p>
</section>

<!-- ─── §02 ─── -->
<section id="s-causes" data-code="causes">
<div class="section-no">02 — Root Causes</div>
<h2>Three Bottlenecks, Measured</h2>
<p>
  SpecForge identifies three independent inefficiencies, each with quantified impact. Understanding which bottleneck dominates at which model scale is key to reading the throughput numbers in §05.
</p>

<div class="vp">
