<p>
  For MoE models the benefit is even larger: the HuggingFace implementation "encounters runtime errors and fails to robustly support large-scale MoE models," making SGLang not just faster but required for stability. SGLang's expert parallelism distributes MoE routing across devices in a manner that ZeRO sharding fundamentally cannot replicate, since ZeRO assumes dense parameter tensors.
</p>
<p>
  The decoupling also solves a maintenance problem: SGLang adds native support for newly released models promptly. SpecForge can immediately train drafts for any model SGLang supports — including Kimi K2 (1T parameters) and Qwen3 — without re-implementing model code.
</p>

