</div>
</section>

<!-- ─── §04 ─── -->
<section id="s-attention" data-code="attention">
<div class="section-no">04 — Sparse Tree Attention</div>
<h2>From 80% Memory Overhead to 6.5% — FlexAttention + In-Place Kernel</h2>
<p>
  EAGLE-3's Training-Time Test runs 7 autoregressive draft steps during training. At each step <em>t</em>, the model attends over the full training prefix (length T) plus all previously predicted token representations (T+1 through t−1). The naive implementation materializes the full attention logit matrix S at each TTT step and holds it for the backward pass — a cumulative O(T²) memory allocation per sample that accounts for 80% of activation memory.
</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">attention-memory.py</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">Drag/click seq_len slider — watch naive memory explode vs FlexAttention</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div style="display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
      <span style="font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted)">seq_len:</span>
      <input type="range" id="seqlen-slider" min="0" max="4" value="4" style="width:200px;accent-color:var(--purple)">
      <span id="seqlen-label" style="font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--purple-l)">4096</span>
    </div>
    <canvas id="attn-canvas" style="width:100%;height:260px;display:block;"></canvas>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:1.5rem;margin-top:.625rem;justify-content:center">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem;font-size:.68rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted2)"><span style="width:14px;height:3px;background:rgba(239,68,68,.8);display:inline-block"></span>SDPA (naive)</div>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem;font-size:.68rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted2)"><span style="width:14px;height:3px;background:rgba(16,185,129,.8);display:inline-block"></span>FlexAttention (SpecForge)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>How FlexAttention Eliminates the Overhead</h3>
<p>
  PyTorch's FlexAttention compiles a custom attention mask (the BlockMask) into a Triton kernel via TorchInductor. Two properties make it ideal for TTT: (1) it computes attention in a FlashAttention-style streaming pass — never materializing the full N×N logit matrix as a stored tensor, and (2) the BlockMask structure precomputes which blocks can be skipped, partially computed, or fully computed, exploiting the causal + suffix sparsity pattern in tree attention.
</p>
<p>
  At sequence length 4096 on a single H200 GPU, switching from SDPA to FlexAttention reduces TTT attention <strong>wall-clock time by 62.1%</strong> and <strong>peak memory by 93.5%</strong>. The gap grows with sequence length because naive memory scales O(seq_len²) while the BlockMask streaming approach scales roughly O(seq_len).
</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">TTT Attention — Naive vs BlockMask Memory</div>
  <span style="color:rgba(239,68,68,.9)">Naive</span>:   S<sub>t</sub> ∈ ℝ<sup>B × H × T</sup>  materialized at each step  →  cumulative <span class="math-var">O(γ · T²)</span><br>
  <span style="color:rgba(16,185,129,.9)">FlexAttn</span>: BlockMask streams attention in tiles  →  <span class="math-var">O(tile_size · T)</span> intermediate memory<br>
  <span class="math-comment">γ = TTT steps (default 7), T = sequence length, B = batch, H = heads</span>
</div>

<h3>In-Place Gradient Kernel</h3>
<p>
  A second complementary kernel eliminates the separate gradient buffer for the masked softmax backward pass. In the standard implementation, after the forward log-softmax loss is computed, the logits tensor is no longer needed — yet a separate gradient buffer is allocated. The custom Triton kernel overwrites the logits tensor <em>in place</em> with ∂L/∂z during the backward pass. This reduces memory overhead by an additional <strong>30–40%</strong> depending on context length and vocabulary size.
</p>

