<section id="s-quality" data-code="quality">
<div class="section-no">06 — SpecBundle: Training Quality</div>
<h2>Better Training → Better Drafts: Up to 4.48× Inference Speedup</h2>
<p>
  SpecForge's training efficiency matters because it makes it practical to train on much larger, higher-quality datasets. Existing open-source EAGLE-3 checkpoints were trained on ShareGPT (120K conversations) or UltraChat (200K) — small, research-oriented corpora. SpecBundle uses Open-PerfectBlend: 1.4M balanced conversations across chat, math, coding, and instruction following, with responses regenerated from each target model (temperature 0.8) to ensure distribution alignment.
</p>
<p>
  The dataset quality difference alone adds 1.17× inference speedup on Math500 for LLaMA-3.1-8B (acceptance length 2.82 → 3.48 tokens). Combined with the SpecForge-trained models, SpecBundle achieves up to <strong>4.48× end-to-end inference speedup</strong> over no speculative decoding and <strong>1.35×</strong> over existing EAGLE checkpoints.
</p>

