    <p>Welcome to this audio summary of SpecForge, focusing on training efficiency for speculative decoding drafters.</p>
    <p>Speculative decoding is a key technique to accelerate LLM inference. It works by having a small draft model generate candidate tokens, which are then verified in parallel by a larger target model. However, training these draft models is traditionally slow and computationally expensive.</p>
    <p>SpecForge addresses this training bottleneck through three major architectural optimizations.</p>
    <p>First, Target-Draft Decoupling. Standard EAGLE training runs both the target and draft models together. SpecForge decouples them. By pre-generating and caching target hidden states, it avoids running the massive target model during draft training. This reduces GPU memory usage and speeds up training by several fold.</p>
